.\" robodr-setup(8). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-ops/src/bin/robodr-setup.rs and the module docs of
.\" crates/robodr-ops/src/{preflight,setup}.rs. Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-SETUP 8 "2026-10-31" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-setup \- first-boot setup of a RoboDR unit: host preflight, keys, role configuration, fingerprints
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-setup preflight
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-min\-free\-mib
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-state\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-keys\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-ignore\-check
.IR ID ]...
.br
.B robodr\-setup keys \-\-unit\-id
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-role
.IR ROLE ]
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR KIND ]...
.RB [ \-\-keys\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B robodr\-setup config \-\-role
.I ROLE
.B \-\-unit\-id
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-site
.IR SITE ]
.RB [ \-\-interface
.IR IF ]...
.RB [ \-\-examples
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR FILE ]
.br
.B robodr\-setup fingerprints
.RB [ \-\-keys\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B robodr\-setup init \-\-role
.I ROLE
.B \-\-unit\-id
.I ID
.RB [ \-\-site
.IR SITE ]
.RB [ \-\-interface
.IR IF ]...
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR KIND ]...
.RB [ \-\-keys\-dir
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-ignore\-check
.IR ID ]...
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.PP
Every subcommand also takes
.BI \-\-root " DIR"
(operate on the file tree under
.IR DIR ,
for image staging and tests; commands such as
.B systemctl
still query the running host).
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replaces the manual first-boot steps of the quick start (requirements,
keys, configuration, key registration) with one checked sequence. Run it
as root after installing the package (the offline bundle installer installs
the units disabled).
.B Nothing that exists is ever overwritten:
an existing key or configuration is kept and reported, so the command can
be re-run safely and can never replace a key the SOC already trusts.
.PP
.B init
runs
.BR preflight ,
and stops with exit 1 (generating and writing nothing) if any check
fails; then
.BR keys ,
.B config
(not for
.BR soc\-relay )
and
.BR fingerprints .
.SH PREFLIGHT
Each check is
.BR OK ,
.B WARN
(RoboDR runs with something reduced),
.B FAIL
(a RoboDR unit cannot run, or would run wrongly) or
.B SKIP
(not applicable to the installed package:
.B robodr\-focal
has no
.BR robodr\-pulsard ).
.TP
.B kernel.btf
.I /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux
or an external BTF
.I /etc/robodr/btf/vmlinux
stamped for the running kernel. WARN without any (no host behaviour
detection; network detection is unaffected); FAIL for an external BTF of
another kernel or without its stamp.
.TP
.B bpffs
.I /sys/fs/bpf
mounted as
.BR bpf .
WARN otherwise
.RB ( robodr\-pulsard
refuses to start).
.TP
.B nf_tables
loaded, built in, a module of the running kernel, or usable through
.BR "nft list tables" .
WARN otherwise
.RB ( robodr\-executor
and
.B robodr\-firewall\-gw
cannot enforce).
.TP
.B systemd
PID 1 is systemd, and the running manager
.RB ( "systemctl show \-p Version" )
is 247 or newer (245 for
.BR robodr\-focal ).
FAIL otherwise. The detail names an installed version that differs from
the running one (reboot to run it). Only when the manager does not answer
is the installed
.B systemctl \-\-version
used, and the detail says so.
.TP
.B glibc
at least the
.B libc6
floor of the installed
.B robodr
package (2.35 when it cannot be read). FAIL otherwise: use
.BR robodr\-focal .
.TP
.B clock
FAIL when the wall clock is before this release was built (evidence and
finding timestamps would be wrong); WARN when not NTP-synchronised.
.TP
.B disk
free space on the file system of
.B \-\-state\-dir
(default
.IR /var/lib/robodr ):
FAIL below
.B \-\-min\-free\-mib
(default 2048), WARN below twice that.
.TP
.B keys.dir
the key directory
.RB ( \-\-keys\-dir ,
default
.IR /etc/robodr/keys )
is a root-owned directory without group or other access. FAIL otherwise;
WARN when missing (the package creates
.IR /etc/robodr/keys ).
.PP
.BI \-\-ignore\-check " ID"
downgrades that check's FAIL to a WARN that says it was ignored (for
example
.B clock
on an isolated lab bench).
.B keys.dir
cannot be ignored.
.SH ROLES
.TP
.B robot
on-robot agent on a ROS 2 companion computer
.RI ( agentd.example.json ).
.TP
.B unitree\-edu
Unitree EDU development computer
.RI ( agentd.unitree\-edu.example.json ).
.TP
.B unitree\-sensor\-box
passive sensor box on a tap or mirror port
.RI ( agentd.unitree\-sensor\-box.example.json ).
.TP
.B soc\-relay
SOC side of an air-gapped site
.RB ( robodr\-diode\-unpack " and " robodr\-uplink
under a
.B relay
key): keys only, no agent configuration.
.SH KEYS
Ed25519 keys in the
.B robodr\-blackbox
key format, written exactly like
.B robodr\-blackbox keygen
does: the secret 0600 (exclusive create, no symlink followed), the public
half next to it as
.I .pub
(0644). The secret is never printed. A directory that group or others can
reach is refused.
.TP
.B blackbox
.I agentd\-blackbox.key
(robodr-agentd's
.BR LoadCredential= ),
bound to the unit id (agentd requires the binding to equal
.BR robot.id ).
An existing one bound to another unit id (a box re-provisioned under a new
id) is refused with exit 1 before any key is written: retire the old key
(move it and its
.I .pub
away, revoke it at the SOC) or use the old id.
The default for every role but
.BR soc\-relay .
.TP
.B finding
.I agentd\-finding.key
(finding signatures; drop-in
.IR 20\-finding\-key.conf.example ).
.TP
.B uplink
.I uplink.key
(robodr-uplink; the
.B relay
key on a SOC relay, its default).
.TP
.B diode
.I diode.key
(robodr-spool-export).
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B config
writes the role's example with the unit id in
.B robot.id
and
.BR sensor.profile_trust.expect_unit_id ,
the site and capture interfaces when given, validated by robodr-agentd's
own parser, to
.B \-\-out
(default
.IR /etc/robodr/agentd.json ,
0640, group
.BR robodr ).
Values that still read like an example are listed for review. Check the
result with
.B robodr\-agentd \-\-check\-config
once the commissioned profile, its trust file and the response policy are
installed.
.SH FINGERPRINTS
For every
.I *.pub
in the key directory: key id, algorithm, device binding,
.B key sha256
(SHA-256 of the 32 raw public key bytes, the same value
.BR robodr\-commission (1)
uses for key revocation) and the SHA-256 of the file. Register the key ids
with the SOC over a channel you trust (read them out, or compare after
copying the
.I .pub
files on vetted media). Secret key files are never opened.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
done (preflight: no FAIL).
.TP
.B 1
a preflight check failed (init: nothing was generated or written), or an
error.
.TP
.B 2
usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/keys/
keys (0700 root).
.TP
.I /etc/robodr/agentd.json
the role configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/share/robodr/examples/
the role templates (agentd configuration per role), read before
.B init
generates any key; kept on minimal images, which drop
.IR /usr/share/doc .
Without
.BR \-\-examples ,
.I /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/
is tried next.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-agentd (8),
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1),
.BR robodr\-commission (1),
.BR robodr\-support\-bundle (8),
.I /usr/share/doc/robodr/customer/quick\-start.md
